    "details": "Cary Phillips reports:\n\n> \\[OpenEXR v3.4.11 is a p\\]atch release that addresses the following\n> security vulnerabilities:\n>\n> - CVE-2026-42217 Shift exponent overflow in\n>   readVariableLengthInteger() (ImfIDManifest.cpp)\n> - CVE-2026-42216 Out-of-bounds read in IDManifest::init() during\n>   prefix expansion\n> - CVE-2026-41142 Integer overflow in ImageChannel::resize leads to\n>   heap OOB write via OpenEXRUtil public API\n> - OSS-fuzz 504280155 Heap-buffer-overflow in DwaCompressor_uncompress\n> - OSS-fuzz 505062709 Null-dereference READ in\n>   Imf_3_3::prefixFromLayerName\n",
